**Note on running this build — not part of the licence text above, and not a
condition of the grant.**

The text above is the whole grant: use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
sublicense, sell, and run it — including removing the access control described
here.

This build separately ships a **technical** access control. `msb-v3` verifies an
owner-signed key at `~/.msb-v3/source-license` before it will start
(`src/msb_v3/__main__.py`; opt-outs `MSB_CONTAINER=1` and `MSB_CI=1`), so an
anonymous clone or API tarball boots nothing until a key is present. That is a
guard in this build, not a restriction attached to the copyright grant.
See `README.md` → "Access & licensing".
